  "problem": "Differentiate ${e}^{x}(2+sin\u2061(x)).$\n\n$({e}^{x}(2+sin\u2061(x)))^{\u2032}=$\n{{field-1}} $+\\,{e}^{x}cos\u2061(x)$",
  "worked_solution": "Here, we have the product of the two functions $u(x)={e}^{x}$ and $v(x)=2+sin\u2061(x).$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({e}^{x}sec\u2061(x))^{\u2032} & ={u}^{\u2032}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{\u2032}(x) \\\\  & =({e}^{x})^{\u2032}\\cdot (2+sin\u2061(x))+{e}^{x}\\cdot (2+sin\u2061(x))^{\u2032} \\\\  & =({e}^{x})(2+sin\u2061(x))+({e}^{x})(cos\u2061(x)) \\\\  & =(2+sin\u2061(x)){e}^{x}+{e}^{x}cos\u2061(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
